# Product and Technical Decisions

Status: DONE
Milestone: M0 Planning foundation
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Resolve decisions that would otherwise cause expensive implementation churn.

## Accepted

- [x] Unity is the production engine.
- [x] Gameplay uses true 3D geometry and collision.
- [x] Presentation targets original low-poly/retro-modern styling.
- [x] First vertical slice is offline.
- [x] First territory implementation is floor-only.
- [x] Prototype remains a separate historical mechanics reference.
- [x] First vertical-slice matchup is Ice versus Fire, with bots required for interaction testing.
- [x] First pressure system is a shrinking safe boundary; closing lanes and rotating score zones are deferred
  experiments.
- [x] Territory authority uses a CPU logical grid for rules/scoring and a GPU mask for visuals, subject to the
  Territory Painting alignment and performance gate.
- [x] First-slice minimum target is 1080p at approximately 60 FPS on GTX 1060/RX 580-class graphics, a
  four-core CPU, and 8 GB RAM.
- [x] Keyboard/mouse and generic Xbox-/PlayStation-style gamepads are required.
- [x] First-slice player disruption is non-lethal: slow, knockback, and temporary disable only.
- [x] Team bank accumulates from contested actions and is displayed, but cannot be spent in the first slice.
- [x] Initial match duration target is two minutes, including shrinking-boundary compression and resolution.
- [x] Working title remains EntropyTag.
- [x] Future expansion includes an original comedic precision-platformer single-player mode built around
  bounce/momentum traversal and hostile-environment slapstick.

## Tasks

